From: FineWine
Subject: [PATCH] Run on stock macOS for Apple Silicon: no x18, no memory below 4 GB.

Windows on ARM assumes two things that macOS only gives a process holding an Apple-issued
entitlement (com.apple.developer.cross-architecture-support, which CrossOver's loader has):

1. Register x18 holds the TEB and survives. macOS clears x18 whenever a thread passes through
   the kernel: page fault, interrupt, signal, context switch. A signal handler cannot restore
   it either.
2. Memory below 4 GB can be mapped. Windows keeps its shared data page at 0x7ffe0000. macOS
   kills an arm64 binary whose __PAGEZERO is smaller than 4 GB and refuses fixed mappings
   below it.

This patch makes Wine's own code work without either:

- NtCurrentTeb() reads the TEB from thread-specific data slot 6, which libpthread reserves for
  Wine. TPIDRRO_EL0 holds the slot array; its low three bits are the CPU number. The condition
  names clang as well as GCC because PE modules are built in MSVC-compatible mode.
- The assembly in ntdll that read TEB fields through x18 (exception and callback dispatchers on
  the PE side; the syscall and unix-call dispatchers on the Unix side) loads the TEB the same
  way, into the register it was about to use. call_user_mode_callback uses its TEB argument.
- The Unix side stores the TEB in the slot when a thread starts (server_init_thread, and
  server_init_process_done for the first thread, which does not go through server_init_thread).
- The shared data page moves to 0x17ffe0000 in the seven places Wine refers to it.
- The loader is linked with the default __PAGEZERO and segment alignment on aarch64.

Limits: code not built from this tree still expects x18 and 0x7ffe0000. Third-party ARM64
programs, and x64 code under an emulator, need those accesses trapped or translated. That is
not part of this patch.
---
diff --git a/configure b/configure
index 8c3c32a..d1f2653 100755
--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -12446,6 +12446,12 @@ else case e in #(
 esac
 fi
         ;;
+      aarch64)
+        # FineWine: macOS refuses to start an arm64 binary whose __PAGEZERO is smaller than 4 GB
+        # or whose segments are not 16K-aligned, so the loader is linked with the defaults.
+        wine_use_preloader=no
+        WINELOADER_LDFLAGS="-Wl,-sectcreate,__TEXT,__info_plist,loader/wine_info.plist"
+        ;;
       *)    wine_use_preloader=no ;;
     esac
 
diff --git a/configure.ac b/configure.ac
index 509522e..64f3919 100644
--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -998,6 +998,12 @@ case $host_os in
             WINELOADER_LDFLAGS="$WINELOADER_LDFLAGS -Wl,-no_pie,-image_base,0x200000000,-no_huge,-no_fixup_chains,-segalign,0x1000,-segaddr,WINE_RESERVE,0x1000"],
            [wine_use_preloader=yes])
         ;;
+      aarch64)
+        dnl FineWine: macOS refuses to start an arm64 binary whose __PAGEZERO is smaller than 4 GB
+        dnl or whose segments are not 16K-aligned, so the loader is linked with the defaults.
+        wine_use_preloader=no
+        WINELOADER_LDFLAGS="-Wl,-sectcreate,__TEXT,__info_plist,loader/wine_info.plist"
+        ;;
       *)    wine_use_preloader=no ;;
     esac
 
